BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 1 of 4) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Silberschatz - Operating System Concepts \(Ch. 8\)) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Chapter 8: Deadlocks) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (8.1 System Model & Foundational Definitions) Tj T* (A computer system consists of a finite number of resources to be distributed) Tj T* (among a number of competing processes. Resources are categorized into several types,) Tj T* (each consisting of some number of identical instances \(CPU cycles, memory, files, printers\).) Tj T* (A process must request a resource before using it and must release the resource after finishing.) Tj T* (A set of processes is in an anomalous deadlock state when every process in the set is waiting) Tj T* (for an event that can only be caused by another process in the set.) Tj T* ET
endstream
