stream
BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 4 of 4) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Silberschatz - Operating System Concepts \(Ch. 8\)) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (8.4 Deadlock Avoidance & The Banker's Algorithm) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (Deadlock avoidance algorithms require that the operating system be given priori information) Tj T* (concerning which resources a process will request throughout its lifetime.) Tj T* (The Banker's Algorithm ensures the system never enters an unsafe state.) Tj T* (A state is considered safe if the system can allocate resources to each process \(up to its maximum\)) Tj T* (in some specified order without ever triggering a deadlock.) Tj T* (Safety check condition: Allocation + Need <= Max resources available.) Tj T* ET
endstream
